---
import "@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/400.css"
import "@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/500.css"
import MarketingLayout from "../components/marketing/MarketingLayout.astro"

export const prerender = true

// One page an investor reads in two minutes. Every figure is one the full fact-check kept: the benchmark range comes
// from the archive docs/benchmarks/vector-efficiency-2026-10 and the brain's from the dated knowledge eval in
// docs/benchmarks/vector-knowledge-2026-10-19 (test/investor-page.test.ts recomputes both), the counts from the shipped
// catalog and agents, and every item that is not live carries its status.
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Vector · Investor one-pager"
  description="Vector, the self-evolving AI agentic harness: a free, neutral workspace for coding agents with its own lean agent, a brain that learns each repository from desktop 1.99.110, and a model of its own in development."
  noindex
>
  <div class="ip-root">
<div class="ip-page">
  <header class="ip-top">
    <div class="ip-brand">
      <span class="ip-mark" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14"><path d="M1.5 2.5 L7 12 L12.5 2.5" fill="none" stroke="#ffffff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
      Vector
    </div>
    <div class="ip-meta"><span>vectordev.ai</span><span>Investor one-pager</span><span>October 2026</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="ip-thesis" aria-labelledby="thesis-title">
    <h1 id="thesis-title">The self-evolving AI <em>agentic harness</em>.</h1>
    <p class="ip-lede">Over a quarter of organisations send different work to different models,<sup>1</sup> yet each lab builds its agent around its own. <strong>Vector is the neutral harness:</strong> its own lean agent beside Claude Code, Codex and Cursor Agent, on any model, and, from desktop 1.99.110, a brain that learns each repository it works in.</p>
    <div class="ip-facts">
      <div class="ip-fact"><strong class="ip-num">67–75%</strong><span>less modelled spend than Claude Code in a first session, offline*</span></div>
      <div class="ip-fact"><strong class="ip-num">219</strong><span>model providers and 8,184 models, plus local ones</span></div>
      <div class="ip-fact"><strong class="ip-num">9K</strong><span>tokens in Vector's first request, against about 30K for Claude Code, offline*</span></div>
      <div class="ip-fact"><strong class="ip-num">$0</strong><span>for the workspace, on desktop and in the terminal</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ip-section" aria-labelledby="now-title">
    <h2 id="now-title" class="ip-eyebrow">Why it is inevitable</h2>
    <div class="ip-reasons">
      <div class="ip-reason">
        <h3>The labs close ranks</h3>
        <p>They sell their own agents and cut others off: Anthropic blocked third-party tools from Claude Pro and Max, and OpenAI says Cursor's access ends on 12 November 2026. Vector runs each lab's own CLI and its own agent on any provider or a local model, so if one door closes the work moves to another.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ip-reason">
        <h3>Good models are cheap and open</h3>
        <p>The price of a given level of performance falls 9x to 900x a year,<sup>2</sup> so the model alone is no moat.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ip-reason">
        <h3>Every token is a line on the bill</h3>
        <p>38% of organisations set usage limits to control AI cost,<sup>1</sup> and the harness decides how many tokens a task takes.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ip-section" aria-labelledby="tech-title">
    <h2 id="tech-title" class="ip-eyebrow">Proprietary technology</h2>
    <div class="ip-road">
      <div class="ip-milestone ip-lead">
        <span class="ip-stage">Desktop 1.99.110</span>
        <h3>Vector Brain</h3>
        <p>Rules, memory, lessons and a team's specs and PDFs in one local graph, linked to the code, with drift flagged and Undo on what it learns. Through code links, 40 of 40 eval tasks got their requirement; keywords alone, 1 of 40.†</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ip-milestone">
        <span class="ip-stage">Today</span>
        <h3>Tokenomics engine</h3>
        <p>Sessions priced from provider-reported tokens wherever the model has a price; in the desktop app, the Run Guard stops a run within one step of the cap you set.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ip-milestone">
        <span class="ip-stage">Today</span>
        <h3>Subagent system</h3>
        <p>Nine built-in subagents, from explore and review to security and migration, run in the background in the desktop app, and their spend counts against the run's cap when one is set.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ip-milestone">
        <span class="ip-stage">Today</span>
        <h3>Vectorscope</h3>
        <p>AI review on GitHub, desktop and CLI, with a verify pass that re-checks blocking findings. No Vector fee.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ip-milestone">
        <span class="ip-stage">In development</span>
        <h3>Vector Velocity</h3>
        <p>A 550B-parameter model built for Vector's own loop, designed to cost significantly less to run than other very large coding models. No weights or benchmarks yet.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ip-milestone">
        <span class="ip-stage">Today · desktop</span>
        <h3>Vector Cloud</h3>
        <p>Previews, rollbacks and migrations on the team's own Vercel and Supabase accounts. The software factory, issue to reviewed preview in the cloud, is planned.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ip-milestone">
        <span class="ip-stage">Built in, not on sale</span>
        <h3>Vector Codium</h3>
        <p>Low-cost coding models on one Vector account, with no provider keys.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ip-split" aria-label="Business model and stage">
    <div class="ip-panel">
      <h2 class="ip-eyebrow">Business model</h2>
      <p class="ip-muted">The free workspace brings developers in. Vector plans to earn where the spend is: <strong class="ip-ink">Codium</strong> credits first, then its own model, then many more cloud services of its own (intent).</p>
      <div class="ip-tiers ip-num" aria-label="Codium plans">
        <span class="ip-tier"><b>$10</b> <span>/ mo</span></span>
        <span class="ip-tier"><b>$50</b> <span>/ mo</span></span>
        <span class="ip-tier"><b>$100</b> <span>/ mo</span></span>
        <span class="ip-tier"><b>$200</b> <span>/ mo</span></span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ip-panel">
      <h2 class="ip-eyebrow">Stage</h2>
      <ul class="ip-clean ip-limits">
        <li><strong>Very early.</strong> Desktop previews since July 2026, free since 4 October 2026; no retention data yet.</li>
        <li><strong>Unsigned installers;</strong> no SOC 2, SSO or admin console yet.</li>
        <li><strong>Built on open source.</strong> The agent core is adapted from an MIT-licensed agent; orchestration, cost, review and the brain are Vector's own.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer class="ip-foot">
    <p class="ip-footnote"><strong>* Benchmark method.</strong> Vector's offline efficiency benchmark, archived at docs/benchmarks/vector-efficiency-2026-10: Vector's runtime at an 11 October 2026 revision (commit 6f7f3c2ea) and Claude Code 2.1.215 performed identical scripted tool steps against a local fake model server, with the same number of model requests, in three fix tasks. Medians of three repetitions at the same list rates ($3 per million input tokens, $3.75 cache write, $0.30 cache read, $15 output), with caching modelled and tokens estimated as characters ÷ 4; a second session, run as a new process, came out 75% lower. It measures what each agent sends, not the quality of answers or a provider's real bill, and it does not show that Vector is cheaper than other agents in general.</p>
    <p class="ip-footnote"><strong>† Knowledge eval.</strong> 19 October 2026, in docs/benchmarks/vector-knowledge-2026-10-19: five short specs for a small invented repository and 58 requests, written alongside the feature; no model call. Not an independent benchmark.</p>
    <p class="ip-footnote"><strong>Privacy.</strong> Vector itself never trains on prompts or code. Requests to free models whose providers don't train ask them not to, and free models whose providers may train are labelled May train on your prompts and sent only after the user accepts that once.</p>
    <p class="ip-footnote"><strong>1.</strong> Stack Overflow 2026 Developer Survey, 6 October 2026. <strong>2.</strong> Epoch AI, LLM inference price trends, 12 March 2025: 9x to 900x a year, depending on the performance level.</p>
    <details class="ip-details ip-sources">
      <summary>Sources, checked 11–17 October 2026</summary>
      <div class="ip-source-groups">
        <div>
          <h4>Market</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="https://stackoverflow.blog/2026/10/06/the-results-of-the-2026-developer-survey-are-here/" rel="noopener">Stack Overflow 2026 Developer Survey</a>, <a href="https://epoch.ai/data-insights/llm-inference-price-trends" rel="noopener">Epoch AI on inference price trends</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://venturebeat.com/ai/anthropic-cracks-down-on-unauthorized-claude-usage-by-third-party-harnesses/" rel="noopener">VentureBeat on third-party tools and Claude, January 2026</a>, <a href="https://www.channelinsider.com/ai/news-openai-cursor-model-access-spacex-acquisition/" rel="noopener">Channel Insider on OpenAI and Cursor</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4>Vector</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="/docs/external-agents">Outside agents</a>, <a href="/docs/tokenomics">tokenomics engine</a>, <a href="/docs/vectorscope">Vectorscope</a>, <a href="/legal/privacy#training">privacy policy on training</a>, <a href="/legal/terms">terms</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </details>
  </footer>
</div>
  </div>
</MarketingLayout>

<style is:global>

  /* Layout: one centred reading column, short enough to read as one page: the thesis and its numbers, why now, the
     technology with its status, then the business and the stage. */
  .ip-root {
    --bg: #0e0c12;
    --surface: #16131c;
    --raised: #1e1a26;
    --ink: #f2eefb;
    --muted: #a59eb4;
    --faint: #6f6880;
    --line: rgba(226, 213, 237, 0.1);
    --line-strong: rgba(226, 213, 237, 0.18);
    --accent: #a48cf0;
    --accent-deep: #7659d0;
    --accent-soft: rgba(164, 140, 240, 0.13);
    --accent-ink: #120d1f;
    --good: #6fcf97;
    --part: #d9ae5f;
    --none: #6f6880;
    --compare: #5d566e;
    --dot: #7d7690;
    --font-display: "Geist Variable", "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
    --font-body: "Inter Variable", "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
    --font-mono: "IBM Plex Mono", ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    color-scheme: dark;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: light) {
    :root:not([data-theme="dark"]) .ip-root {
      --bg: #f6f4fa; --surface: #ffffff; --raised: #f0edf6; --ink: #17131f; --muted: #5b5469; --faint: #8b8498;
      --line: rgba(20, 16, 30, 0.1); --line-strong: rgba(20, 16, 30, 0.18);
      --accent: #6548c9; --accent-deep: #5a3fc0; --accent-soft: rgba(101, 72, 201, 0.09); --accent-ink: #ffffff;
      --good: #23864f; --part: #9a6c14; --none: #9c97a6; --compare: #b9b3c4; --dot: #8b8498;
      color-scheme: light;
    }
  }
  :root[data-theme="light"] .ip-root {
    --bg: #f6f4fa; --surface: #ffffff; --raised: #f0edf6; --ink: #17131f; --muted: #5b5469; --faint: #8b8498;
    --line: rgba(20, 16, 30, 0.1); --line-strong: rgba(20, 16, 30, 0.18);
    --accent: #6548c9; --accent-deep: #5a3fc0; --accent-soft: rgba(101, 72, 201, 0.09); --accent-ink: #ffffff;
    --good: #23864f; --part: #9a6c14; --none: #9c97a6; --compare: #b9b3c4; --dot: #8b8498;
    color-scheme: light;
  }

  .ip-root { min-height: 100vh; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.55; -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }
  .ip-page { max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto; padding-inline: 20px; padding-block: 32px 48px; display: grid; gap: 36px; }
  .ip-page > * { min-width: 0; }
  .ip-root h1, .ip-root h2, .ip-root h3, .ip-root h4 { font-family: var(--font-display); margin: 0; text-wrap: balance; letter-spacing: -0.015em; }
  .ip-root p { margin: 0; }
  .ip-root sup { font-size: 0.7em; color: var(--faint); }
  .ip-eyebrow { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11.5px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); }
  /* Section labels are h2s for the outline, set as eyebrows. */
  .ip-root h2.ip-eyebrow { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11.5px; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: 0.12em; }
  .ip-muted { color: var(--muted); }
  .ip-ink { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .ip-small { font-size: 13.5px; }
  .ip-mono { font-family: var(--font-mono); }
  .ip-num { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }

  /* Header */
  .ip-top { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding-bottom: 16px; }
  .ip-brand { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 800; font-size: 20px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .ip-mark { width: 26px; height: 26px; border-radius: 7px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #7659d0 0%, #8b6ce3 38%, #a287ef 70%, #c0acf9 100%); display: grid; place-items: center; }
  .ip-mark svg { display: block; }
  .ip-meta { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); display: flex; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap; }

  /* Thesis */
  .ip-thesis { display: grid; gap: 18px; }
  .ip-thesis h1 { font-size: clamp(32px, 5.2vw, 54px); font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.04; max-width: 21ch; }
  .ip-thesis h1 em { font-style: normal; background: linear-gradient(100deg, #7659d0 0%, #8b6ce3 40%, #b39cf4 100%); -webkit-background-clip: text; background-clip: text; color: transparent; }
  .ip-thesis .ip-lede { font-size: 17px; color: var(--muted); max-width: 66ch; }
  .ip-thesis .ip-lede strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .ip-facts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; background: var(--surface); }
  .ip-fact { padding: 14px 16px; display: grid; gap: 2px; border-left: 1px solid var(--line); min-width: 0; align-content: start; }
  .ip-fact:first-child { border-left: 0; }
  .ip-fact strong { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 26px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .ip-fact span { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .ip-facts { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } .ip-fact:nth-child(3) { border-left: 0; } .ip-fact:nth-child(n+3) { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); } }

  /* Section heads */
  .ip-section { display: grid; gap: 18px; min-width: 0; }
  .ip-section-head { display: grid; gap: 6px; }
  .ip-section-head h2 { font-size: clamp(22px, 3vw, 28px); font-weight: 700; }
  .ip-section-head p { color: var(--muted); max-width: 72ch; }
  .ip-section-head p b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }

  /* Lists */
  ul.ip-clean { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 10px; }
  ul.ip-clean li { padding-left: 16px; position: relative; }
  ul.ip-clean li::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.62em; width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 2px; background: var(--accent); }


  .ip-footnote { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--faint); max-width: 92ch; }
  .ip-footnote strong { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 500; }

  /* Reasons */
  .ip-reasons { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 12px; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .ip-reasons { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }
  .ip-reason { border-top: 2px solid var(--accent); padding-top: 12px; display: grid; gap: 6px; align-content: start; min-width: 0; }
  .ip-reason h3 { font-size: 16.5px; font-weight: 700; }
  .ip-reason p { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--muted); }

  .ip-details { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted); }
  .ip-details summary { cursor: pointer; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11.5px; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); width: fit-content; }
  .ip-source-groups h4 { font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .ip-source-groups ul { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 4px; }

  /* Proprietary technology: a grid of cards, each with its status. */
  .ip-road { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; background: var(--surface); }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .ip-road { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }
  .ip-milestone { padding: 18px; display: grid; gap: 8px; align-content: start; border-left: 1px solid var(--line); min-width: 0; position: relative; }
  .ip-milestone:first-child { border-left: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .ip-milestone { border-left: 0; } .ip-milestone:nth-child(n+2) { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); } }
  .ip-milestone::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: 0; height: 3px; background: linear-gradient(90deg, #7659d0, #a287ef); opacity: 0.85; }
  .ip-milestone h3 { font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700; }
  .ip-milestone p { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--muted); }
  .ip-stage { display: inline-block; justify-self: start; vertical-align: middle; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 999px; padding: 1px 8px; }
  .ip-stage.ip-intent { border-style: dashed; }
  .ip-milestone.ip-lead { grid-column: 1 / -1; border-left: 0; background: linear-gradient(160deg, var(--accent-soft), transparent 70%); }
  @media (min-width: 761px) { .ip-milestone.ip-lead ~ .ip-milestone { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); } .ip-milestone.ip-lead ~ .ip-milestone:nth-child(3n + 2) { border-left: 0; } }
  .ip-milestone.ip-lead h3 { font-size: 21px; }
  .ip-milestone.ip-lead p { font-size: 14.5px; max-width: 86ch; }
  /* Business + stage */
  .ip-split { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 28px; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .ip-split { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }
  .ip-panel { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px; background: var(--surface); display: grid; gap: 12px; align-content: start; min-width: 0; }
  .ip-tiers { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .ip-tier { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12.5px; padding: 6px 10px; border-radius: 8px; background: var(--raised); border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .ip-tier b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 500; }
  .ip-tier span { color: var(--muted); }
  .ip-limits li { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--muted); }
  .ip-limits li strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  ul.ip-limits li::before { background: var(--part); }

  /* Footer and sources */
  .ip-foot { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 16px; display: grid; gap: 10px; }
  .ip-sources { color: var(--faint); }
  .ip-source-groups { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 16px 24px; padding-top: 12px; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .ip-source-groups { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }
  .ip-source-groups li { font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .ip-root a { color: var(--accent); }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .ip-root * { transition: none !important; animation: none !important; } }
</style>
